use flake

# `use flake` (nix-direnv) only watches flake.nix and flake.lock. But the
# `sandboxed-ai` package this flake builds also embeds the launcher (sandbox.sh)
# and the seatbelt profiles (*.sb) via its src fileset, so editing any of them
# changes the derivation. Watch those too — modern nix-direnv makes watch_file
# participate in its cache, so a change rebuilds the dev shell rather than
# reloading into the stale cached one (this is why nix_direnv_watch_file is now
# deprecated in favour of watch_file).
#
# nullglob so a missing *.sb can't leave the literal "*.sb" in the list; the glob
# re-expands on every reload, so profiles added later are picked up automatically
# once any watched file triggers a reload.
shopt -s nullglob
watch_file sandbox.sh *.sb
shopt -u nullglob
